WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.702
Used as shipped, the two products fall
short of the loop in four places,

2
00:00:04.702 --> 00:00:07.150
and Gate 2 closes two of them on paper.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.021
Gap two: with SailPoint's
Service Catalog app,

4
00:00:10.021 --> 00:00:13.977
requests follow the approval
process defined in ServiceNow,

5
00:00:13.977 --> 00:00:19.330
while the Federal Modernization Workbook's
design decides owner-governed access,

6
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:23.287
classes A two and A three, in
the identity governance platform.

7
00:00:23.287 --> 00:00:27.051
Gate 2 answers with one approver
system per authority class.

8
00:00:27.051 --> 00:00:29.887
Gap four: two doors into the directory.

9
00:00:29.887 --> 00:00:34.886
SailPoint can provision Entra ID and
Active Directory, while the workbook's

10
00:00:34.886 --> 00:00:40.362
design makes Entra inbound provisioning
the one writer of HR-mastered attributes.

11
00:00:40.362 --> 00:00:43.324
Gate 2 answers with one
writer per attribute.

12
00:00:43.324 --> 00:00:47.437
It also gives each operation class
a lane and a change-record type.

13
00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:50.350
Every later gate builds
what this one decides.
